      "description": "Watch West Ham vs Portsmouth highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling night of football on August 8, 2026, as West Ham United hosted Portsmouth in a highly anticipated Carabao Cup fixture. Fans gathered in anticipation of a classic cup tie, with both teams eager to prove their worth and secure a place in the next round of the competition. Early Pressure and the Opening Blow Portsmouth entered the contest with no fear, immediately testing the Hammers' resolve. After an early flurry of corners and a blocked attempt from Colby Bishop , the visitors found their breakthrough in the 33rd minute. Following a corner, Adrian Segecic pounced on a loose ball outside the box and unleashed a precise left-footed strike into the bottom left corner, leaving Mads Hermansen with no chance and giving the underdog supporters a reason to dream. However, the lead acted as a wake-up call for West Ham United , who responded with a devastating scoring burst late in the first half. In the 43rd minute, Mohamadou Kanté found Valentín Castellanos in the center of the box, and the striker made no mistake, firing into the top right corner. The momentum shifted entirely when, in stoppage time, Jarrod Bowen took center stage. Assisted by Pablo , Bowen struck a powerful left-footed effort from distance to flip the game on its head and send the hosts into the break with a 2-1 lead. Castellanos Seals the Deal The second half began with the Hammers looking to put the game out of reach, and they did exactly that in the 50th minute. Jarrod Bowen turned provider, delivering a pinpoint cross that Valentín Castellanos met with a powerful header into the center of the goal. The brace for Castellanos gave West Ham United a comfortable two-goal cushion and forced Portsmouth into a series of tactical changes, including a triple substitution that saw Odin Bailey and Marezi enter the fray. Despite the deficit, Portsmouth continued to fight, with Adrian Segecic forcing another save from Hermansen and Eoin Kenny missing a narrow chance from the center of the box. As the clock wound down, West Ham managed the game professionally, with James Ward-Prowse and Joël Veltman adding fresh legs to the midfield and defense. Pablo nearly added a fourth in the final minute, hitting the post, but the 3-1 scoreline remained intact, confirming a professional and well-earned victory for the London side."
